From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?The=20wider=20screen:=20the=20trainer's=20throw?=
 =?UTF-8?q?,=20the=20Pok=C3=A9dex=20page's=20flashing=20(SDK=5FPORT=5F3DS)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The player's (and the opponent's) trainer, sliding off after throwing
the ball, is taken away only once all of it is past the wider screen's
edge (battle_display.c, PORT_TRAINER_REACH: the sprite reaches 60 pixels
on from its position; at the DS's -40 less the wider screen's 32, 20
pixels of the player were still showing when it went).

The Pokédex's page after a catch: its background shows no hand-drawn
picture (WIDE_NO_ART, port_wide_layout.h): as the header blinks, its art
is at times the info page's, whose built-in picture is laid out as that
page is, and the page flashed between the two.
---
 include/port_wide_layout.h               |  1 +
 src/applications/pokedex/ov21_021E8D48.c |  6 ++++++
 src/battle/battle_display.c              | 11 ++++++++---
 3 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/port_wide_layout.h b/include/port_wide_layout.h
index 8ffa9c72..db1564b3 100644
--- a/include/port_wide_layout.h
+++ b/include/port_wide_layout.h
@@ -59,6 +59,7 @@ extern void NitroPort_WindowFramed(const void *window, int frame);
 #define WIDE_PICTURE(bg, picture, x, y, angle)    { 5, WIDE_BG(bg), (y), (y) + 1, (x), (x) + 1, (angle), (picture) }
 #define WIDE_CLEAR(bg, pal, mask)                 { 6, WIDE_BG(bg), 0, 1, 0, 1, (pal), (mask) }
 #define WIDE_SHOW(bgs, top, bottom)               { 7, (bgs), (top), (bottom), 0, 1, 0, 0 }
+#define WIDE_NO_ART(bgs)                          { 8, (bgs), 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0 }
 
 // The pictures (their files: <name>.png; the port's numbers, in
 // 3ds_port/nitro/include/nitro_port_wide.h, are the same).
diff --git a/src/applications/pokedex/ov21_021E8D48.c b/src/applications/pokedex/ov21_021E8D48.c
index 4349954f..6eaad902 100644
--- a/src/applications/pokedex/ov21_021E8D48.c
+++ b/src/applications/pokedex/ov21_021E8D48.c
@@ -86,6 +86,12 @@ static const short sPokedexRegisterWideLayout[][8] = {
     WIDE_MOVE(WIDE_BG(3), 24, 120, 248, 256, 88 - 248),
     WIDE_SHIFT3D(-24),
     WIDE_OBJS(14, 62, 96, 256, 24),
+    // (2026-10-26) the background without a hand-drawn picture: as the
+    // header blinks, its art is at times the info page's, whose picture
+    // (built in: fedf88a75a541576) is laid out as that page is (the frame
+    // where the DS has it, the text box wider), and the page flashed
+    // between the two
+    WIDE_NO_ART(WIDE_BG(3)),
 };
 #endif
 
diff --git a/src/battle/battle_display.c b/src/battle/battle_display.c
index 02095d20..439dc697 100644
--- a/src/battle/battle_display.c
+++ b/src/battle/battle_display.c
@@ -81,10 +81,15 @@
 
 #ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
 // (the 3DS remaster's wider upper screen: a trainer sliding off the screen
-// gone once past its edges, not the DS's)
+// gone once past its edges, not the DS's. The sprite reaches 60 pixels on
+// from its position (its cells, 2026-10-26: the player's back sprite at
+// -67 still showed 20 pixels of its right side in the wider screen's left
+// band), and the DS's -40 left 20 of it on the DS's screen, where the cell
+// test hid it: here it's gone only once all of it is past the edge.)
 extern int NitroPort_WideScreenExtra(void);
-#define PORT_TRAINER_GONE_LEFT  (-40 - NitroPort_WideScreenExtra())
-#define PORT_TRAINER_GONE_RIGHT (256 + 40 + NitroPort_WideScreenExtra())
+#define PORT_TRAINER_REACH      64
+#define PORT_TRAINER_GONE_LEFT  (-PORT_TRAINER_REACH - NitroPort_WideScreenExtra())
+#define PORT_TRAINER_GONE_RIGHT (256 + PORT_TRAINER_REACH + NitroPort_WideScreenExtra())
 #else
 #define PORT_TRAINER_GONE_LEFT  -40
 #define PORT_TRAINER_GONE_RIGHT (256 + 40)
-- 
